.env.*
# ...but NOT the templates. They carry no secrets, and they are the only
# record of which variables a deploy has to set. Ignoring them is why a CI
# checkout had no NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL to copy and the production build
# failed on a variable nobody knew was required.
# frontend/.env.example only: it holds public NEXT_PUBLIC_* values and no
# credentials. backend/.env.example stays ignored — the secret scanner
# rejects it (DATABASE_URL and JWT_SECRET are credential-SHAPED even as
# placeholders), and a template that teaches people to commit a line
# starting JWT_SECRET= is the wrong habit to encode.
!frontend/.env.example
